# Test: a web user deleted from the config cannot log in after a reload, and
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
#       cannot keep using a session cookie issued before it
# VALIDATES: web authentication answers from the RUNNING config on BOTH credential
#            paths. A user the operator removes and reloads stops authenticating
#            at once with a password (AC-1) and with an already issued session
#            cookie (AC-10), and the user the same reload keeps still
#            authenticates on both (AC-2, AC-12).
# PREVENTS: a deleted web account living on until the daemon restarts. Two copies
#           of the user list produced that. The fallback authenticator held the
#           list built when the web server started, and it was consulted exactly
#           when the live AAA chain REJECTED a login -- so the current config said
#           no and the startup copy said yes. The cookie branch of
#           AuthMiddlewareWithAudit held the second: it validated only the 24h
#           TTL and never consulted any user list, so an open tab kept full
#           config-edit rights for the rest of the day. The reload reported
#           success either way, leaving the operator no signal.

option=timeout:value=90s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/web-user-removed-by-reload:timeout=90s
expect=exit:code=0
